      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So as I replied to Tom Ley, it could be rolled out to only trusted users at first and mitigated by only allowing an event a week like where I can't upload a world everyday. I have to wait a week. Also, can have recurring events. I think if the devs think along these lines, they could mitigate a lot of the people creating meetings every second of every day. There are solutions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
