      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60f27ab54dc3b21b95ac9e76|full_name} I want to say the events/calendar feature should be available to all groups and all users, no special requirements. But discovery could have some algorithmic constraints: events created by trusted groups and users might have greater weight than brand-new groups or events created by new users; events too far out or scheduled too close to them happening could be (temporarily) suppressed; groups that frequently schedule events would be deprioritized; events at PC-only worlds shouldn't be promoted to Android/Quest players (even if they're in the group for it)... and of course, abuse can be reported, even if most people won't see it.\n\nedit: I think a relatively high limit to fight general spam (10 events per week, per group/user in whatever combination) might also be nice, but that's really just for server resource purposes.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
